<section class="section section--flush-top">
  <div class="container split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">What smart forms does</p>
      <h2>One form engine, four kinds of field work.</h2>
      <p>Paper forms and static PDFs are the weak link in field data — questions that don't apply, handwriting re-keyed later, no way to route a failed inspection until someone remembers to call it in. Smart Forms behaves like software: it adapts to what's entered, pulls known data instead of asking twice, and moves the next step along on its own.</p>
      <p>The same engine runs every kind of field capture — and because field work doesn't stop where cell coverage does, it all works fully offline.</p>
      <ul class="tags"><li>Visual inspections</li><li>Work orders</li><li>Testing</li><li>Regulatory forms</li></ul>
    </div>
    <div class="capability-media">
      <img src="/static/img/forms/sync-status.webp" width="530" height="267" alt="Sync status while offline: 14 forms queued, 0 records lost, 2 minutes since last sync. Queued: 9 inspections, 4 work orders, 1 regulatory form." loading="lazy">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--surface">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2>Built-in intelligence, not add-on logic.</h2>
      <p>Every form carries the same four capabilities — none of them require a separate tool or a workaround.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="capability">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">01 — Logic</p>
        <h3>Conditional show/hide logic</h3>
        <p>Follow-up fields appear only when the answer calls for them. Shorter forms, fewer wrong answers, and nothing irrelevant to scroll past on a phone screen in the rain.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/forms/conditional-logic.webp" width="531" height="346" alt="Leak inspection logic: Leak observed? answered Yes and shown; Estimated leak rate revealed by Yes and required; Repair already attempted? hidden until a leak is confirmed." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="capability capability--flip">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">02 — Data</p>
        <h3>Data-driven dropdowns</h3>
        <p>Fields pull live from the asset registry and prior records — ID, location, history — instead of free text a technician has to remember or guess. Select the asset, and the form already knows it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/forms/data-driven-dropdowns.webp" width="531" height="288" alt="Asset lookup for Skid A-114, auto-filled from the registry: location Cedar Ridge Plant, last inspection Jul 29, 2026, criticality High." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="capability">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">03 — Routing</p>
        <h3>Dispatch, escalation &amp; multi-step workflows</h3>
        <p>A completed form can trigger the next step on its own: dispatch a work order, escalate a failed inspection, or route a regulatory form for sign-off — no one has to remember to follow up.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/forms/dispatch-workflow.webp" width="531" height="266" alt="Workflow for FORM-2281: form submitted offline at 9:47 AM (done), escalated to supervisor because the leak rate is above threshold (in progress), work order dispatched (queued, waiting on escalation)." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="capability capability--flip">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">04 — Offline</p>
        <h3>Offline-first field capture</h3>
        <p>Forms work with zero signal — no internet, no cell data, no exceptions for remote sites. Everything syncs automatically the moment connectivity returns.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/forms/offline-capture.webp" width="531" height="318" alt="Field tablet 04, offline since 8:52 AM with 3 forms pending sync: 2 inspections and 1 work order captured. They will sync automatically when signal returns, with no re-entry required." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

